Project: Threes helper – live preview tracker
=============================================

Purpose
- Mac helper that watches the mirrored iPhone Threes window, detects the “next” tile preview (red/blue/gray or large-candidate band), and maintains 12-tile (4/4/4) and 24-tile (one large) state to display odds.

Current files (in repo root)
- preview_detector.py: image/array/PIL detector. Outputs {red, blue, gray, large_candidates}. Finds preview crop via saturation near upper center. Exposes classify_array / classify_pil / classify_image.
- preview_detector.py also exposes board ROI helpers: find_board_roi, board_signature (low-res quantized fingerprint), board_signature_diff.
- window_stream.py: default mode listens to arrow keys (Quartz event tap) and captures on each press; shows remaining small tiles as colored squares (🟥/🟦/⬜️) plus `P(large)=x%`. Hotkeys: Z undo last move, Q reset to a fresh game (immediate capture seeds the new cycle). Small pool: 4/4/4 resetting every 12 non-large tiles; large pool: 1 per 24 small tiles (inserted in addition). Optional polling mode with `--poll` still available; board change threshold tunable via --board-delta-threshold (default 0.3). Arrow capture delay defaults to 0.03s (`--arrow-delay`). Auto-selects the first window whose title starts with `iPhone Mirroring` (override with --auto-window-prefix). Frontmost fallback if enumeration fails; if auto-pick fails it will list windows for manual selection, then fallback to frontmost. `--board-once` snapshots the 4x4 board + preview (🟥/🟦, blanks=`·`, gray/others=`X`); `--dump-tiles <dir>` writes the 16 cell crops + preview for segmentation debugging.
- README.md: usage, permissions, and run commands.
- Screenshots currently present: 'Screenshot 1.png', 'Screenshot 2.png', 'Screenshot 3.png', 'Screenshot 4.png'. (Earlier files with “Screenshot 2025-11-19 at 4.12.xx PM.png” existed; if needed, ensure sample images are available for classification tests.)

Dependencies / permissions
- Python libs: Pillow, numpy present. Install Quartz bindings for best results: `python -m pip install pyobjc-framework-Quartz` (use your Python path, e.g., /opt/homebrew/anaconda3/bin/python).
- macOS permissions: Screen Recording (for screencapture) and Accessibility (for AppleScript fallback).

How to run now
- Screenshot test:
  python3 - <<'PY'
  import glob, subprocess
  for path in glob.glob('Screenshot*PM.png'):
      print(f'=== {path}')
      subprocess.run(['python3','preview_detector.py','--image',path,'--debug'], check=False)
  PY
- Live polling (pick a window):
  python3 window_stream.py --poll-seconds 0.4
  - Choose the Threes/iPhone-mirroring window from the numbered list.
  - Add --print-all to log every poll.
  - If “No windows found,” press Enter, then click/focus Threes within 3 seconds; it will grab the frontmost window.
  - If Quartz is missing, install pyobjc-framework-Quartz; otherwise it falls back to System Events (may fail for iPhone Mirroring).

Recent blocker and mitigation
- AppleScript/System Events often fails to get window id for “iPhone Mirroring” (-1728). Mitigation: use Quartz enumeration/capture via pyobjc-framework-Quartz. Frontmost fallback remains but relies on System Events if Quartz is missing.

Game logic assumptions (for upcoming state engine)
- Each 12-tile span: exactly 4 red, 4 blue, 4 gray; reset after 12.
- Each 24-tile span: exactly one large tile randomly placed; may appear adjacent across spans.
- Start tracking at game start (tile 1). Preview shows next small tile color or large band (three options); we only need color vs large-band flag.

